& [SJS]
  + Situation: the completed lookup and quotation path is callable as a CLI but a model host must know process syntax and parse an undocumented command surface
  + Justification: the repository already has a proven read-only MCP server and can expose a second strict tool without modifying llama.cpp hidden state or the resident service
  + Solution: prepare immutable anchor artifacts once in embedded mode and add one simple discovery-described lookup_sop_anchors tool beside unchanged query_sop

& [ArchitectureDecision]
  + reuse CantorMcpServer rather than create another process or transport
  + add an optional embedded-only AnchorLookupRuntime containing environment digest admitted fabric catalogue and lexical sidecar
  + do not add the tool to resident mode because doing so would require a new service operation and broader authority
  + dispatch get_tool list_tools and call_tool by exact name and advertise only operations available in that backend

& [ContractDecision]
  + strict arguments are text include_source maximum_postings and maximum_matches
  + include_source defaults true because direct inspectability is the intended tool use and can be explicitly disabled for a smaller payload
  + structured output retains the complete core lookup and source projection forms without translating their proof semantics
  + short text content describes status only and structuredContent remains authoritative

& [SecurityAndHonesty]
  + startup uses the exact existing preflight and admission path and every call replays core results
  + tool metadata declares read-only idempotent closed-world behavior
  + the adapter mints only a deterministic request identifier from exact text and never mints caller authority scope package bindings or effects
  + lexical and snapshot non-authority statements remain present in core results
  + resident unavailability is visible through tool discovery rather than runtime fallback

& [TestDecision]
  + embedded metadata tool list direct execution repeatability source-default source-disable strict argument and budget faults
  + resident tool list excludes lookup_sop_anchors and direct attempted execution refuses
  + existing query_sop exact core equivalence and real process tests remain green
  + real stdio MCP process over tracked corpus returns exact admitted Cantor quote through the new tool

& [Disposition]
  + [status] ready_for_exact_phase_lock
  + [still_locked] service_protocol_semantic_gating_provider_attention_effect_and_compiler_backends
